<GuideLayout 
  title="The 5-Point Quality Control Checklist for Activewear Brands"
  type="QUALITY CONTROL"
  description="Standardize your quality expectations. From stretch tests to seam strength, ensure your manufacturer meets global standards."
>
  <p>Ensuring consistent quality is the biggest challenge for growing activewear brands. At Fitclo, we implement a rigorous 5-point QC process.</p>
  <h3>1. Fabric Inspection</h3>
  <p>Every roll of fabric is tested for color fastness, shrinkage, and four-way stretch before cutting begins.</p>
  <h3>2. Sample Verification</h3>
  <p>Pre-production samples must be signed off to ensure every detail matches your tech pack.</p>
  <h3>3. In-Line Inspection</h3>
  <p>Our QC team monitors the sewing lines daily to catch stitching issues early.</p>
  <h3>4. Measurement Audit</h3>
  <p>We check final products against the size chart to ensure fit consistency.</p>
  <h3>5. Packaging & Final Check</h3>
  <p>Final inspection ensures trimming, labeling, and folding meet retail-ready standards.</p>
</GuideLayout>
